Open Geo Datasets — licence
===========================

The boundary, name, label-point and area data in this repository is derived from
Natural Earth, which is in the PUBLIC DOMAIN.

    "All versions of Natural Earth raster + vector map data found on this website
     are in the public domain. You may use the maps in any manner, including
     modifying the content and design... Crediting the authors is unnecessary."
     — https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/

Accordingly, the maintainers of this repository place their own contributions
(the build scripts, the France region dissolve, the computed areas and repaired
label points, the file layout) into the public domain under CC0 1.0:

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

WHAT THIS MEANS FOR YOU

  - Commercial use: permitted.
  - Redistribution, including inside a closed-source mobile app: permitted.
  - Shipping derived data offline (region name, ISO code, a label lat/lng):
    permitted.
  - Attribution: NOT required, in-app or anywhere else.
  - Share-alike: does NOT apply.

  A credit is welcome but is not a condition of use. If you would like to give
  one, "Made with Natural Earth" is the phrase Natural Earth suggests.

PER-FILE EXCEPTIONS

  Not every file in this repository is public domain. The French administrative
  reference data (INSEE codes, chef-lieu, commune and postal-code files) comes
  from data.gouv.fr under the Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0, which DOES
  require attribution.

  See PROVENANCE.md for the source and licence of every file. Check it before
  redistributing anything from france/communes.* or france/codes-postaux.*.
